virglrenderer: Venus devices always get robust buffer access

What: vkr_dispatch_vkCreateDevice turns on robustBufferAccess (in
VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 when the guest chains it, else in pEnabledFeatures)
whenever the host device offers it, whatever the guest asked for. Without it
the host's Vulkan driver logs once.
Why: a guest Vulkan app chooses its buffer ranges; without robust buffer access
an out-of-range vertex, index, uniform or storage access reaches the GPU as
told. On Apple's GPUs a fault resets the GPU (on 2026-10-04 that hung
WindowServer and panicked macOS). The GL path checks ranges itself (ADR 0017);
Vulkan has a driver feature for it, so it is asked for. Not shown to protect
anything: MoltenVK reports the feature on every Apple GPU, and no test has made
an out-of-range Vulkan access to see it contained (that would have to run on the
real GPU, STANDARDS 14). The cost was not measured either.
Upstream: OmacVM policy (a host may rather trust its guests); not sent.
Tests: tests/graphics venus runs (vkmark, deqp.sh vk) on a Venus runtime; the
log line tells when a host device lacks the feature.
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device.c
@@ -173,6 +173,38 @@
 
    ((VkDeviceCreateInfo *)args->pCreateInfo)->ppEnabledExtensionNames = exts;
    ((VkDeviceCreateInfo *)args->pCreateInfo)->enabledExtensionCount = ext_count;
+
+   /* Robust buffer access is on whenever the host device offers it, whatever the guest
+    * asked: without it the GPU fetches out-of-range buffer addresses as told, and on
+    * Apple's GPUs a fault there resets the GPU (on 2026-10-04 that panicked macOS). The
+    * create info is the decoder's copy, so it can be changed. */
+   VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures supported;
+   VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures robust_features;
+   memset(&supported, 0, sizeof(supported));
+   vk->GetPhysicalDeviceFeatures(physical_dev->base.handle.physical_device, &supported);
+   if (supported.robustBufferAccess) {
+      VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 *features2 = NULL;
+      for (VkBaseOutStructure *s = (VkBaseOutStructure *)args->pCreateInfo->pNext; s;
+           s = s->pNext) {
+         if (s->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_FEATURES_2)
+            features2 = (VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 *)s;
+      }
+      if (features2) {
+         features2->features.robustBufferAccess = VK_TRUE;
+      } else {
+         if (args->pCreateInfo->pEnabledFeatures)
+            robust_features = *args->pCreateInfo->pEnabledFeatures;
+         else
+            memset(&robust_features, 0, sizeof(robust_features));
+         robust_features.robustBufferAccess = VK_TRUE;
+         ((VkDeviceCreateInfo *)args->pCreateInfo)->pEnabledFeatures = &robust_features;
+      }
+   } else {
+      static bool warned;
+      if (!warned)
+         vkr_log("the host Vulkan device has no robust buffer access");
+      warned = true;
+   }
 
    struct vkr_device *dev =
       vkr_context_alloc_object(ctx, sizeof(*dev), VK_OBJECT_TYPE_DEVICE, args->pDevice);
